    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d650">

                <pb facs="0940" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg812"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">820.7961 Dept. of Commerce Flight/13:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Bolivia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Cottrell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-20T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 20,
                                1928—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2. Department’s No. 1, January 7.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d650-f1"/> Department of
                    Commerce states that Duke Banks is local representative of the Curtiss Airplane
                    and Motor Corporation and desires Legation and Consulate to cooperate with him
                    in promoting interest in American aircraft products and aeronautics in Bolivia.
                    Please comply and inform Consulate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
